==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|ekes out|eking out|eked out}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[supplement]].
#: ''The old man '''eked out''' his pension by selling vegetables from his garden.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[obtain]] with [[difficulty]] or [[effort]].
#: ''He '''eked out''' a living selling vegetables from the garden.''

